    "claim": "Command exposure model (check_security): with security on, a command executes anonymously only if BOTH the library meta's readers and the command record's readers contain 'anonymous'; otherwise the session user's groups must intersect the command's readers, and the 'admin' group always passes. Empty readers on a command record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.",
    "tags": "platform-api,security,readers,groups",
    "source": {
